1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is a time known as
the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:55,257
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:58,477
Raise the sails and take the helm!

18
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,897
That the end of the map reveals?

20
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,717
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,117
Till someone proves it real!

22
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,577
Through it all.

23
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,477
Through all the trouble and times.

24
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

25
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,537
Know that I will be there.

26
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:21,277
To stand by you.

27
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:24,260
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

28
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

29
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,560
All your hopes and dreams.

30
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,877
Together we will find everything.

31
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,020
That we're looking for.

32
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you.

33
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,460
If you wanna be my friend?

34
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,780
We are, we are on a cruise.

35
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

36
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:58,517
Oh right they want to fight too huh?

37
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,697
Now this will be fun!

38
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:04,257
Okay pops you promised me remember.

39
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:07,577
If I run those pirates off
then my debt to you is clear!

40
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,697
No more chores that's the deal.

41
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,897
There's no telling how much more of my

42
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,980
restaurants you could screw
up if you stick around.

43
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:20,857
Yeah so kid you said you were going to
be king of the pirates were you serious?

44
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:25,900
If we can capture that ship, the Grand
Line will be ours for the taking.

45
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:32,000
No more pretending to be Marines or
raising the white flag of surrender.

46
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:36,957
None of our enemies will suspect that
we're a threat with a ship like that.

47
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:39,860
In that boat, it'll
always be a sneak attack.

48
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:41,410
He's right.

49
00:02:41,493 --> 00:02:42,937
That boat would come in handy.

50
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:46,837
No one would think that pirates were
on such a ridiculous-looking ship.

51
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:47,920
Right, but Don,

52
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,377
even if we enter the Grand
Line again using that vessel,

53
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,297
what if we come across someone
like Hawkeye Mihawk again?

54
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:55,615
Then what will we do?

55
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:04,480
I really appreciate the input,
sailor. Anything else? No! No!

56
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:09,040
Do you think an ordinary man could
cut up a sailing ship like that?

57
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:13,360
That man probably has the
power of the Devil Fruit.

58
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:18,140
Although those with Devil Fruit
powers are rare and legendary to us,

59
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:21,460
I assure you they're
commonplace on the Grand Line.

60
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:26,837
Mihawk must have used some sort of strange
power when he sliced our ship to ribbons.

61
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:30,449
When we're on the Grand Line,
those powers won't be special.

62
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:33,780
Even the Straw Hat Freak
will be considered normal.

63
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:38,040
That old geezer Redfoot Zeff
sailed those seas for a year.

64
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:46,252
It stands to reason that he had strategies
for dealing with those monsters.

65
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,717
The techniques for
surviving that parade of

66
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,677
weirdos must be written
in the old man's logbook.

67
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:56,937
Along with clues to the One Piece.

68
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:59,357
I see, you're a genius.

69
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:02,337
All we have to do is get
that logbook in the ship.

70
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:05,117
Then we'll be able to find our
way to the One Piece again.

71
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,437
You hear that, boys?

72
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,160
Now let's get to it!

73
00:04:08,340 --> 00:04:09,987
The restaurant will be ours!

74
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:15,115
You pirate scum are gonna
have to get through us first!

75
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:18,940
Go to the control room and
open up the fins. What? No!

76
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,620
That's a bad idea!

77
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,677
If we do that, we'll be
giving the enemy a foothold!

78
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,995
And that's just fine.

79
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:28,417
We gotta do whatever it takes to
keep those guys out of this place.

80
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:32,077
If they destroy the inside, then
the old man will complain forever.

81
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,336
Did you just say something, you brat?

82
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,960
Yeah, I said you're whiny now go yes, sir!

83
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:09,397
Did you see that go kid?

84
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,037
What the heck's up with that guy?

85
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,517
Yeah, he's crazy!

86
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,637
It's hard to believe!

87
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:16,737
The Grand Line is crawling
with guys like these.

88
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:22,057
Sanji, pay special attention
to how this one fights!

89
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:26,037
So let me get this straight: you're
attacking the restaurant that gave you food.

90
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,037
I got no choice but To
beat some manners into you!

91
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:34,057
So you want to fight on the water
where there's no place to stand?

92
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:39,380
Huh a bold move for someone like you the
Devil Fruit has taken your ability to swim.

93
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,920
Hasn't it your boy? Yeah, but now

94
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,959
Now we have somewhere to fight him.

95
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:20,810
Whoa!

96
00:06:20,893 --> 00:06:21,723
That's so cool!

97
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:28,555
My cooks and I will never
give up defending this place.

98
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,420
Prepare to die. I see.

99
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:33,996
Good plan, bringing up all
that extra decking, genius.

100
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:37,269
Now we don't have to
take the fight inside.

101
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:39,940
I'd hate to damage my future ship.

102
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,760
And make no mistake, it will be mine!

103
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:45,680
We will never let you have the restaurant!

104
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:46,920
That's right!

105
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,280
We mean business!

106
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,953
We're battle cooks now!

107
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:02,320
Sanseo Mackerel Head One,
the Baratie's secret weapon!

108
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:06,280
So, if you want to live, I
suggest running away now!

109
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,420
What is that thing?

110
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,240
That thing is so cool!

111
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:15,400
Paddle faster!

112
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:16,760
You paddle faster!

113
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,470
Fire!

114
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:28,580
Those guys are gonna sink
me too! Yeah! Get him!

115
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:30,450
Yeah!

116
00:07:30,533 --> 00:07:31,363
Get him, guys! Get him!

117
00:07:31,446 --> 00:07:32,276
Blow them away!

118
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:33,320
You can do it!

119
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,290
Nice!

120
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,037
Keep your eyes on the prize, Patty!

121
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,061
This one counts!

122
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,050
Right!

123
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:46,240
Krieg, say your prayers!

124
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:49,757
Little did you know that
the Sea Restaurant Baratier

125
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:53,134
had such a powerful weapon
just waiting to be unleashed!

126
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,400
What happened?

127
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:04,817
Did we bump into something?

128
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:05,900
We're not moving!

129
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,540
I am Don Creed!

130
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:12,320
The man who will rule the oceans!

131
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,500
Oh no you're not! I am!

132
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:17,180
I don't have time for these stupid games!

133
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:18,680
Get out of here!

134
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:23,560
No way!

135
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:24,820
He's so strong!

136
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,840
It's coming straight for us!

137
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,580
The restaurant! Oh, no!

138
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,380
Salute!

139
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,080
No way!

140
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,060
He's got legs of steel.

141
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:15,754
He kicked back that crazy
boat just like it was nothing.

142
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,240
Very impressive.

143
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,670
Nice kick.

144
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,600
What's the deal?

145
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:26,857
Are you trying to crush your friends?

146
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:27,770
Yeah, yeah.

147
00:09:27,853 --> 00:09:30,337
Don't yeah, yeah us, you crazy fool.

148
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:32,180
Stop acting so cool!

149
00:09:32,340 --> 00:09:35,557
You wouldn't be so smug if we'd
been killed, you bucket of backwash!

150
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:36,699
All right, ladies.

151
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:39,457
You think you could wrap
this up another time?

152
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,380
We have business to attend to.

153
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,050
Got them!

154
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,227
You guys still don't get it.

155
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,957
Even well-armed, you're still just cooks,

156
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:57,317
and we're expert fighters that
are way out of your league.

157
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:01,157
So why don't you be good little cooks
and run along to a safer restaurant,

158
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,577
maybe one on land, huh?

159
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:03,600
Come on, guys.

160
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:06,037
Why are you letting them
beat you up so easily, huh?

161
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:08,767
And you still call
yourselves fighting cucks.

162
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,797
Well, these pirates are really good.

163
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:13,397
They're totally different from
the ones we fought before.

164
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,774
It's insulting to lump us in
with that average riffraff.

165
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:21,137
We are the Great Creek Pirates, and we're
the absolute rulers of the East Blue.

166
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:24,257
Let it be known to all that
this garish boat already

167
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:27,164
belongs to the great and
powerful Creek Pirates.

168
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:28,230
You know what?

169
00:10:28,313 --> 00:10:29,797
I've been a cook all my life.

170
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,797
I've worked at a lot of
restaurants and gotten

171
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,980
fired from them all for
scuffling and living hard.

172
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:38,631
And after years of wondering,
we finally found a home here.

173
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,080
Anybody here?

174
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:45,377
This is the restaurant that's owned
by a guy named Redfoot Zef, right?

175
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,677
Hey, we found this damn
Cook's Wanted sign.

176
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:48,590
Is it true?

177
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,180
Yeah, it's true.

178
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:59,400
But you need to understand that
this is no ordinary restaurant.

179
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:03,467
It really doesn't matter who
they are or where they come from.

180
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:07,597
If someone comes in hungry, we will
feed them until they're stuffed.

181
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:09,460
Do I make myself clear?

182
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:12,360
Can you handle that? Sir!

183
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:21,417
I wouldn't serve anyone's slap like this!

184
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:24,100
Hey, what'd you go and hit me for, huh?

185
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,929
Sure victory, sure defeat.

186
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:31,460
We like fighting and cooking, so this
place is perfect for us. That's right.

187
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:33,581
There's no other place like this.

188
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,700
You hear that?

189
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,762
Now that's true fighting spirit.

190
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:42,342
Committing ourselves to cooking fine cuisine
day in and day out is a fierce battle.

191
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:45,460
Compared to that, these
pirates are nothing.

192
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:48,357
He's right, yeah. Let's fight.

193
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,440
Protect Zep!

194
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:51,840
Protect the respawn!

195
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:04,910
Huh?

196
00:12:04,993 --> 00:12:05,859
The hell was that?

197
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:16,360
Just what do you guys think you're doing?

198
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:18,880
Who's that?

199
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,737
So let's do this!

200
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:26,617
But before we begin, it's only fair.

201
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,677
I give you a warning.

202
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,157
I am Pearl the Invincible Shield!

203
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:33,417
Hey, it's Pearl Perona Carney!

204
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,330
Are you boys?

205
00:12:34,413 --> 00:12:37,077
Okay, I'd say that pair is far from okay!

206
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,377
Those two just experienced
my Pearl Surprise!

207
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,637
One of my signature punches!

208
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,014
You bumbling, pathetic

209
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:44,530
idiot!

210
00:12:44,613 --> 00:12:45,597
Hey, look at that!

211
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:46,977
Nice knife!

212
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:48,877
I think I'll take it! What?

213
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,217
Here!

214
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:51,757
Come on! Let it go!

215
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,497
I said, give it to me!

216
00:12:53,580 --> 00:13:00,580
That

217
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,370
guy

218
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:08,283
knows how to

219
00:13:08,366 --> 00:13:09,196
kick some serious butt!

220
00:13:09,279 --> 00:13:11,417
A kitchen knife is a
cook's soul! How dare?

221
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:15,717
Why are you filthy pirates trying to
desecrate one with your grubby little hands?

222
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,630
Sanji.

223
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:19,240
Just stay down and hang on to this.

224
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,180
I'm gonna teach these bozos a lesson.

225
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:27,127
You must be out of your mind if you think
we're gonna be beaten by a mere cook!

226
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:37,764
I'll show you mere cook after I
fillet every one of you bastards.

227
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:39,930
Ha!

228
00:13:40,013 --> 00:13:42,817
How very impudent of you to defeat
them all using only your kicks,

229
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,606
am I to be impressed by that?

230
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,500
I'm a cook, remember?

231
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:50,237
I couldn't do my job very well
if I ruined my hands in battle,

232
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,740
so I'll be taking you down with my feet.

233
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,060
Is that so?

234
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,200
I think not.

235
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,052
I'm invincible, you see.

236
00:13:57,240 --> 00:14:01,100
I've won all 61 of my battles
completely and totally unscathed.

237
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,097
It's quite remarkable, really.

238
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:07,060
No one has ever shed a single drop
of my blood in battle. No one.

239
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,580
Now do you realize my power?

240
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,640
I may be a gentleman, but I'm not gentle.

241
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,190
Got it?

242
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,680
Was that supposed to be a joke?

243
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,517
Because it wasn't even a little bit funny.

244
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:24,953
Dropping your gun is a good
way to end up dead, you brat!

245
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:34,432
Even battleship cannons don't work on me.

246
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,600
I come out of any attack unharmed.

247
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,056
Boy, that could have been really bad.

248
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:44,613
Good thing I didn't fall into the ocean.

249
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:52,920
Oh, this isn't good. Blood! No!

250
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,612
Hey, Pearl, don't worry.

251
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:56,377
It's only a nosebleed, Pearl.

252
00:14:56,460 --> 00:15:00,420
We know it's not a battle
wound, so just keep calm, okay?

253
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:01,820
What's this?

254
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:04,997
These people are just
mean. They're dangerous.

255
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:08,137
So, uh, want to tell me why
everyone's freaking out?

256
00:15:08,220 --> 00:15:10,600
They're worried about a nosebleed?

257
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,400
Calm down!

258
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,180
It's just a nosebleed!

259
00:15:16,340 --> 00:15:17,297
Don't lose your cool!

260
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:18,210
Relax!

261
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,960
Jeez, what is that guy doing?

262
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:25,960
Danger! Danger! Danger!

263
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:33,317
Who knew it started?

264
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,220
When he gets upset, he catches fire!

265
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:37,960
Uh, wait, what?

266
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,260
Fire pearls!

267
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,200
Special treats!

268
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:54,540
Perish in my flames!

269
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:58,080
With my shields and this
inferno, I am invincible!

270
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:01,657
That moron!

271
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:04,328
We need that ship and
he's gonna destroy it.

272
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:09,397
We're either gonna burn or drown.

273
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,337
He's destroying our only ship.

274
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:12,250
This isn't good.

275
00:16:12,333 --> 00:16:13,997
The rest one's gonna catch fire.

276
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,840
Not on my watch!

277
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,040
Burn you!

278
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:25,560
Let you torch our dreams?

279
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:32,840
That guy's either brave or dumb.

280
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:34,700
That cook is gonna burn.

281
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,900
But these flames scare everyone away.

282
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:44,080
Well, if I was scared of fire,
I wouldn't be much of a cook.

283
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,080
I hate him.

284
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,100
I hate that refined gentleman.

285
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,060
Whoa, he got him good!

286
00:16:56,380 --> 00:16:59,439
Yeah, he just broke through
Pearl's invincible wall!

287
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,160
You stupid cook!

288
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,880
You're totally insane!

289
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:09,300
I'll kill you!

290
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:11,350
Fire!

291
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,660
Need more fire!

292
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,280
Fire, Pearls!

293
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:16,730
No!

294
00:17:16,813 --> 00:17:18,367
The whole boat's gonna burn!

295
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:21,657
If the blaze gets to the
kitchen, the ship will explode!

296
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:24,160
Run, Zaf! Get out of there! Run!

297
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:37,240
What? No way!

298
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:38,949
He put out my fire pearls!

299
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,200
Fire pearls, eh?

300
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:41,340
That's kid stuff.

301
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,617
Wow, the gust from his kick
put out all of those flames!

302
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:45,530
Impossible!

303
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,737
I don't believe it!

304
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:49,408
Redfoot Zef is still
just as strong as ever!

305
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,957
Way to go, Pops!

306
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:51,880
I'm impressed!

307
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:54,957
So, then it's finally
come down to this, huh?

308
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,200
I've got no choice.

309
00:17:56,340 --> 00:17:58,281
Smash the fins or the boat burns!

310
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:03,540
Sanji, watch out!

311
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,580
He can't escape!

312
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,192
He's surrounded by fire!

313
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,380
Ouchie! The char boy!

314
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,580
Gum-Gum! Let's go!

315
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:22,260
He tossed that thing right back! Fire hot!

316
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:38,940
Carol is down!

317
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:40,777
And he's not gonna get out this time!

318
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:41,690
No!

319
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:42,830
Pearl!

320
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,080
So weird.

321
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:46,320
Yeah, that guy sure is goofy.

322
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,297
You want something done right?

323
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:50,733
You got no choice but to do it yourself.

324
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:59,780
The battle ends right here.

325
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:17,660
As a kid, I never stopped
searching for a great treasure.

326
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:25,120
I had a map in my mind
that I knew would leave me.

327
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:32,120
I had to find my way to that place
before someone could beat me.

328
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:38,580
The promised land was in my
grasp and I wouldn't let go.

329
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:44,157
My only dream.

330
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:49,317
I won't stop chasing

331
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,080
it until it comes true!

332
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:56,817
But if the world ever

333
00:19:56,900 --> 00:20:00,957
changes I call out your name.

334
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:07,137
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

335
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:11,540
As long as I'm with you

336
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:14,537
my memories won't fade.

337
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:19,620
Waiting for that one true dream?
